// proves: a derive over a gathered enum reads, through `payload_of`
// on the enum's own module, every record and enum its variants name
// that the module exports — `Elem`, `Shape` — and cannot read `Far`,
// which only the member's file imported. A generic derive therefore
// sees exactly the types its own file can name, and answers a type it
// cannot read loudly instead of by a table keyed on a name.
use core.{reads}

println(reads())

"done"
